      "content": "You are absolutely right, as many art historians have observed, that this shift has led to a significant polarization in contemporary art markets and critical discourse. While certain high-impact political works have achieved critical success and high resale values, a noticeable \"crisis of craft\" has developed where purely aesthetic engagement is often judged as a failure of political communication. Ultimately, the value of a work by 2024 increasingly depends on its power to champion a specific cause rather than the technical mastery or visual allure of the piece itself.",
